# [DD-13b.W1.3] AN `export` NAMING A GROUP THE DEFINITION DOES NOT DECLARE.
#
# The check cannot live at the `export` line: `export` names GROUPS and the
# `.rxt` head reader does not parse patterns. It happens at BIND time, where
# the sub-parse's own `named_groups` is in hand, and names BOTH the export and
# the definition — a reader shown only the name cannot tell a typo in the
# export list from a group that was renamed inside the pattern.
target = t

pattern ^(?&piece)$
name t

pattern (?<kept>a)
name piece
export nosuch
